{
  "dom_id": "step-e409",
  "name": "Example: Evaluating the Definite Integral of a Polynomial Function",
  "problem": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_0^4 x \\, \\textrm d x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1+1}}{1+1}{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
